	(text "LANE BUS OUT -> LaneModule #1 J3 (male) via straight 2x5 IDC ribbon (female/female). Pin n -> pin n.\nSame pinout as LaneModule J2. SCL/SDA = I3C1 (PA9/PA8, AF2) like on the lanes.\n47R series on every signal (protection + source termination for push-pull I3C; 47R 0603 already in stock).\nPull-ups go to LANE_3V3 (switched) so nothing back-powers the lanes when LANE_PWR_EN is off.\nFIRMWARE: drive SCL/SDA/SYNC/CHAIN_OUT low or Hi-Z while LANE_3V3 is off (else ~30 mA through lane ESD diodes)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.432 39.624 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a16ab738-65ea-4254-a327-512f8b3e82cc")
	)
	(text "UART_Ext J302: 1 EXT_PWR_EN (PA5), 2 EXT_PWR_FAULT (PA4), 3 GND, 4 UART2_RX (PA3), 5 UART2_TX (PA2), 6 GND, 7 UART4_RX (PA1), 8 UART4_TX (PA0).\nNames are from the board side: board TX -> host RX. 3.3 V logic only, no supply pin. PA1 is NOT 5 V tolerant: level-shift or divide a 5 V Arduino TX.\nSPI_Ext J303: 1 3V3, 2 GND, 3 SCK, 4 GND, 5 MOSI, 6 CS1, 7 CS2, 8 MISO."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 159.004 60.198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fbbb0587-b075-42ba-b61f-8541b72a4de2")
	)
